llowing.  Print this out if you can, its long <br>
<br>
1.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Highlight the following, right click and copy it, Open Microsoft Word, right click and paste.  Or if you dont have MS Word, write it all down on paper, character for character.<br>
<br>
&lt;img src=&quot;______________________&quot; width=&quot;224&quot; height=&quot;163&quot;&gt;&lt;BR&gt;<br>
Your Name&lt;BR&gt;Your Level&lt;BR&gt;Your Server<br>
ICQ #11111111<br>
<br>
2.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Find the picture that you want to use and alter it with in paint, adobe, whatever to adjust the size…. Save it as a Jpeg (.jpg) if you can<br>
<br>
3.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Go to www.facelink.com and create a user account (right hand side of page), write down all of the information so that you can change it later if you so choose.<br>
<br>
4.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Once you have logged on to facelink, select option one (upload your photo)<br>
<br>
5.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Scroll down and you will see the browse button, use this to go to your hard drive and select the image that you have chosen for you signature.<br>
<br>
6.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Here is the fun part, I’m not sure if there is an easier way but this works for me.  Right click the image in the middle of the screen.  Select Properties.  There will be a URL address of the image.  Highlight the URL address and hit copy.<br>
<br>
7.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Next go to the word document that I told you to create in step one.<br>
<br>
8.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Highlight the underlined portion, right click and hit paste, if you do this right it will replace the underline with the URL of your image that you posted to www.facelink.com and copied in step 6.<br>
<br>
9.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Replace the other parts of the text, like your name, your level, your server, ICQ number, you can enter in anything here as long as you don’t mess with the spaces or other thing, (unless you know what you are doing) Once you have done this highlight all of the text, right click and hit copy.<br>
<br>
10.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Now you have your signature built, this step we will post it to EZBoard. Logon to any of the EZBoards, I use Abyss because that is my guild.  On the left hand side near the top you will see a Link to my control center. Click that.<br>
<br>
11.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Click the Edit Preference button. Scroll down and you will see a place for custom Signature.  Right click and select paste, your text (signature) should appear here now.  Right below that, click the use custom signature block.<br>
<br>
12.&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Go back to you favorite EZBoard and try it out, you don’t have to post a message to see if it works, just select preview next to the post message button and then hit post.  It will show you everything, if it works, you will see it.  If it’s not good hit back and start at step 1.<br>
<br>
I’m not an expert, if this doesn’t work, I am sorry and I probably cant help you fix it, unless it something simple.  <br>
<br>
If you think I posted something that doesn’t work, email at dolejh@home.com and Ill change it, this works for me.<br>
<br>
I spent about an hour and a half writing this to try to help people, so please be gentle, this is a generic signature, but will help you learn, and then you can be creative, and try something else.<br>
<br>
<br>
